abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. The one-sided hidden CHSH measures of Eq. (9) of Ducuara, Susa and Skrzypczyk (arXiv:2406.03945), the largest normalized CHSH value when only one party applies an invertible local filter, are solved for every two-qubit state. After whitening the filtering party, the supremum is the maximum of an explicit quadratic over a compact set. With whitened data c, D and A = DD^T, K = A - |c|^2 I, C = [Dc]_x, alpha = tr A - |c|^2, one-sided violation requires alpha > 1, and there the squared supremum is tr A - lambda_min(A + C K^-1 C), attained by an explicit invertible filter; violation occurs exactly when this exceeds one. Other states have value at most one, given by at most four algebraic candidates. Lean proves the supremum, the criterion and the formula for actual density matrices, arbitrary invertible filters and arbitrary qubit observables. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
keywords:
